\f3\b \cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Elvi were artists and scientists reborn, \cb3 eagerly brain-dumping to the limit\cb1 , gobbling down science texts and jamming their brains with libraries of information, \cb3 expanding their appreciation of the elegant complexity and unlikelihood of existence.\cb1  A nation of evolutionary abominations fearlessly jumping to the defence of Darwin. Their souls, filled with the joy of simply being alive, crooned the praises of reason to anyone who would listen, their songs as uplifting as they were solemn. \cb3 Sales continued to shoot upward, to heights previously unknown. Elvi concerts always sold out,\cb1  the message of The Dawkins and the imminent arrival of his replacement, the one-after-the-one, receiving wild applause and unquestioned acceptance. The ovation would always be accompanied by the crowd screaming in maniacal unison, \'93Dawks, Dawks, Dawks.\'94 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The popularity of the Elvi drew no official attention from \cb3 the Directorate of Moral Observance for a very long time\cb1 . Conformity to the laws of business and adherence to the social hierarchy, ensured the distribution of wealth always flowed upward and the shit always flowed down. Respect was only permitted to look up and was always to be returned with scorn. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>At first glance, the Elvi served this purpose very well. Considered as only one entity and unable to claim individual royalties or accumulate sufficient wealth to wield any individual power, they were ripe for exploitation. Deprivation of economic advancement was usually sufficient to crush any fanciful dreams of social climbing and even if there were one hundred thousand of them jitter-bugging around the Dominion, no Elvis would wield power.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Fans of the Elvi, \cb3 the Dawks\cb1 , saw themselves as a benign, loosely affiliated group of wildly enthusiastic music fans that, for the most part, did not really care about social change, the environment or some dude that might get born in the future. About the only seditious act they indulged in was pasting 
\f2\i \cb3 \'93The one-after-the-one is coming\'94
\f1\i0 \cb1  posters on any and every vertical surface that would readily accept glue. A few appeared on walls here and there, but before long, the posters became ubiquitous. \cb3 The Pale was transformed into a thicket of papier-m\'e2ch\'e9 monoliths\cb1 , gathered together in praise of The Dawkins and silently awaiting the one-after-the-one. Where most saw a collection of useless, drug fucked stoners, the \cb3 Moral Compliance Directorate \cb1 saw the Dawks representing doctrinal divergence of the worst kind, an organised threat to the natural order.\
